blurb: The South Portland Board of Education held a budget workshop for the FY2026
  school year, where Superintendent Tim Metheny presented his proposed budget centered
  on declining enrollment and a significant district office reorganization. The meeting
  featured extensive board discussion and public comment on controversial cuts to
  student-facing positions, administrative roles, and a contentious proposal from
  the teachers' union.
